EDuke32's game code is under the GNU General Public License, version 2, in
gpl-2.0.txt. Its Build engine is under Ken Silverman's Build licence, in
buildlic.txt, which allows free use and distribution only and requires its
credits. Many packagers treat the combination as not distributable. The
bundled libraries (Dear ImGui, loguru, smmalloc, minicoro, LZ4, ENet's
declarations and others) carry their licences in their source files. The
patched files remain under their original licences. The program links the
Pyxis SDL2 port statically; SDL2's zlib licence is SDL2-LICENSE.txt.

An image containing EDuke32 is for the person who built it, with their own
game data, and must not be shared. Ordinary images, CI and bundles never
contain it.

The build leaves out OpenGL, Polymer, audio codecs, network play, mimalloc
and the startup window. SDL2 has no audio here, so the game is silent.
